{
  "wireMagic": "pb3",
  "pens": [ {
  
  } ],
  "wsWinStyles": [ {
  
  } ],
  "wpWinPositions": [ {
  
  } ],
  "events": [ {
    "tStartMs": 1290,
    "dDurationMs": 4510,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "The pistol and mantis shrimps are both crustaceans\nthat snap their claws and perform magic."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 5800,
    "dDurationMs": 2440,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Well, at least a sound and light show: the\njet of water squeezed out from between their"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 8240,
    "dDurationMs": 5120,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "claws travels at such speeds that it cavitates\n- the liquid water under negative pressure"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 13360,
    "dDurationMs": 3000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "is literally pulled apart into bubbles of\nwater vapor."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 16360,
    "dDurationMs": 4020,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "When the bubbles collapse in on themselves,\nthey give off a loud \"snap,\" and amazingly,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 20380,
    "dDurationMs": 1930,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "a small flash of light."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 22310,
    "dDurationMs": 3990,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "The shrimp use the sonic shock wave to stun\nor kill prey, but physicists are far more"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 26300,
    "dDurationMs": 4200,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "interested in the flash of light, because\nwe still don't exactly know why it happens."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 30500,
    "dDurationMs": 3660,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Collapsing bubbles can also be created in\na laboratory simply by using sound - since"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 34160,
    "dDurationMs": 4200,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "sound, as we know, is basically just molecules\nrepeatedly pushing against each other and"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 38360,
    "dDurationMs": 3630,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "then pulling apart, if the sound waves are\nintense enough, the low pressure will again"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 41990,
    "dDurationMs": 4220,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "be low enough to pull the liquid apart into\nvapor and cause cavitation bubbles."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 46210,
    "dDurationMs": 3980,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "The bubbles then collapse, and under certain\ncircumstances, they produce light even brighter"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 50190,
    "dDurationMs": 1000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "than the shrimp."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 51190,
    "dDurationMs": 4430,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "This phenomenon of turning sound into light\nis called \"sonoluminescence.\""
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 55620,
    "dDurationMs": 4470,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "We know that the light flashes are incredibly\nshort - lasting only about 100 picoseconds"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 60090,
    "dDurationMs": 4349,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "- and are surprisingly high energy, meaning\nthe collapsing bubbles may be up to 10 times"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 64439,
    "dDurationMs": 2001,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "hotter than the surface of the sun."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 66440,
    "dDurationMs": 4320,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "We don't know for sure, though, how the inside\nof the bubble gets that hot, or what exactly"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 70760,
    "dDurationMs": 1360,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "is giving off the light."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 72120,
    "dDurationMs": 4370,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "The bubble collapses so quickly that the gases\ninside are heated by compression, but the"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 76490,
    "dDurationMs": 3680,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "increased pressure might also cause water\nvapor in the bubble to rapidly condense back"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 80170,
    "dDurationMs": 2840,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "to a liquid, releasing large amounts of latent\nheat."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 83010,
    "dDurationMs": 4710,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And the flash itself might come from glowing\nred-hot Argon or Xenon gas in the air bubble,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 87720,
    "dDurationMs": 4620,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "OR from heat tearing water vapor apart into\nhydroxide and hydrogen ions which then recombine"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 92340,
    "dDurationMs": 3779,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and give off light, OR from the whole interior\nof the bubble getting hot enough to become"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 96119,
    "dDurationMs": 3540,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "a glowing plasma - OR it might be a combination."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 99659,
    "dDurationMs": 4231,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Either way, the cool thing about sonoluminescence\nis that it's still not fully understood despite"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 103890,
    "dDurationMs": 4510,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "being fairly simple to create - I mean, you\ncan buy a basic sonoluminescence kit off the"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 108400,
    "dDurationMs": 1000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "web!"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 109400,
    "dDurationMs": 1829,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Or just get a pet mantis shrimp."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 111229,
    "dDurationMs": 5551,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "If you want to hear about more unexplained\nphenomena in science, a whole bunch of youtubers"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 116780,
    "dDurationMs": 4370,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "like vsauce, veritasium, thebrainscoop, and\nso forth have made videos about \"unanswered"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 121150,
    "dDurationMs": 4200,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "science questions\" which you can find listed\nin the \"All Time 10s\" video of the same name."
    } ]
  } ]
}
